    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 25th with a primary offensive engine fueled by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (75.59). **Yordan Alvarez** provides our highest floor and ceiling, benefiting from a +15% SP skill boost against Melton and an elite 0.449 xwOBA that makes him an auto-start despite the league\u2019s strict efficiency requirements. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains our premier utility for category scarcity; facing a pitcher with a slow delivery provides a 4% bump to his already elite sprint-speed upside. **Junior Caminero** (70.81) and **Trea Turner** (66.52) also anchor the top-half of the lineup, with **Trea Turner** leveraging a prime leadoff spot and favorable matchup against Cavalli to maintain his high-efficiency profile.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Carson Benge** (39.99), who narrowly missed our 40-point threshold for active participation. While his leadoff projection provided a +10% boost, the confluence of a 3.38 xERA opposing starter and a negative platoon matchup against Boyd effectively capped his output, forcing us to bench him to preserve our limited game caps. Meanwhile, **Lars Nootbaar** (60.52) secured a start due to a strong platoon edge (+11%), though we are monitoring a 42% rain risk in his contest; should the weather worsen, he remains our most volatile asset. We continue to manage our bench depth\u2014including **Christian Yelich**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Rece Hinds**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Zac Veen**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, **Jose Fernandez**, and **Pedro Ramirez**\u2014to ensure that only players meeting our strict efficiency metrics are burning through our seasonal limits. \n\nWe are also watching **Colt Keith** (61.75) closely; he benefits from a rare +7% platoon advantage today against Imai, providing much-needed stability alongside **Kazuma Okamoto** (58.34). While **Dillon Dingler** (47.54) and **Caleb Durbin** (45.35) hover near the lower end of our starting floor, their roles in the 3rd and 6th spots respectively provide sufficient R and RBI leverage to justify inclusion. Provided the weather holds for **Lars Nootbaar**, the Zebras are well-positioned to capitalize on these specific SP-skill advantages.",
